an><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mycale was fought in 479 BCE at Mount Mycale on the coast of Ionia, opposite Samos.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-plataea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Plataea</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 479 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Plataea was fought in 479 BCE in Boeotia, where an allied Greek army led by Sparta defeated the Persian land forces under Mardonius.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-eurymedon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-eurymedon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Eurymedon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 466 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Eurymedon was a double victory won around 466 BCE by the Delian League under Cimon over the Persian Empire at the mouth of the Eurymedon river in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-oenophyta"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Oenophyta</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 457 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Oenophyta was fought in Boeotia in 457 BCE, about two months after the Spartan victory at Tanagra.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tanagra"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tanagra</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 457 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tanagra was fought in 457 BCE near Tanagra in Boeotia, Greece, between Athens with its allies and a Spartan-led army returning from central Greece.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-coronea-447-bc"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Coronea (447 BC)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 447 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Coronea of 447 BCE was fought in Boeotia, where Boeotian exiles and their allies defeated an Athenian force under Tolmides as it withdrew.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leucimme"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Leucimme</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 435 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Leucimme was a naval battle fought in 435 BCE off the promontory of Leucimme on Corfu, in which the fleet of Corcyra defeated a Corinthian fleet.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sybota"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sybota</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 433 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sybota was a naval battle fought in 433 BCE near the Sybota islands, off the coast of Epirus, between Corinth and its allies and Corcyra, supported by an…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-idomene"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Idomene</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 426 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Idomene was fought in 426 BCE in Amphilochia, north-western Greece, during the Peloponnesian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sphacteria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-sphacteria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sphacteria</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 425 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sphacteria was fought in 425 BCE on the island of Sphacteria, which closes the bay of Pylos in Messenia, during the Peloponnesian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-delium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-delium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Delium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 424 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Delium was fought in 424 BCE near Delium on the Boeotian coast during the Peloponnesian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mantinea-418-bce"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mantinea (418 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 418 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mantinea of 418 BCE was the largest land battle of the Peloponnesian War, fought in Arcadia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-abydos"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Abydos</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 411 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Abydos was a naval battle of the Peloponnesian War fought in 411 BCE in the Hellespont off the city of Abydos.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-notium"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Notium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 406 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Notium was a naval battle of 406 BCE near Notium, the port of Colophon, close to Ephesus, in the Peloponnesian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-aegospotami"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Aegospotami</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 405 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Aegospotami was a naval battle in 405 BCE on the Hellespont, near Sestos.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cunaxa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-cunaxa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cunaxa</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 401 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cunaxa was fought in 401 BCE on the Euphrates north of Babylon between the Persian king Artaxerxes II and his younger brother Cyrus the Younger, who…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/second-persian-invasion-of-greece.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Second Persian invasion of Greece</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 480 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Persian invasion of Greece was the massive campaign launched by Xerxes I of the Achaemenid Empire in 480 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-peloponnesian-war"><span class="enc-name">First Peloponnesian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · c. 460–445 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Peloponnesian War was fought from about 460 to 445 BCE between Athens and its allies and the Peloponnesian League led by Sparta, together with Corinth and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-sacred-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/second-sacred-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Second Sacred War</span><span class="enc-type">War · c. 449–448 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Sacred War was a brief conflict around 449–448 BCE over control of the sanctuary of Delphi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peloponnesian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Peloponnesian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 431–404 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Peloponnesian War was fought from 431 to 404 BCE between Athens and its empire and the Peloponnesian League led by Sparta.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-expedition"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sicilian-expedition.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sicilian Expedition</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 415–413 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sicilian Expedition was the Athenian invasion of Sicily during the Peloponnesian War, launched in 415 BCE on the pretext of aiding Segesta against Selinus and aimed…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/decelean-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/decelean-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Decelean War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 413–404 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Decelean War, also called the Ionian War, was the final phase of the Peloponnesian War, from 413 to 404 BCE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ionian-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ionian Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 499–493 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ionian Revolt was a rising of the Greek cities of Ionia and other parts of Asia Minor and Cyprus against Persian rule, from 499 to 493 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/inaros-ii"><span class="enc-name">Inaros II</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · d. c. 454 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Inaros II was a Libyan prince who led a revolt against Persian rule in Egypt from about 460 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-cyrus-the-younger"><span class="enc-name">Revolt of Cyrus the Younger</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 401 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Revolt of Cyrus the Younger was a rebellion in 401 BCE in which a Persian prince hired Greek mercenaries to seize the throne from his brother Artaxerxes II.</span></a></li></ul></section>
